 :result
 "Planning is 3.55x faster on IC09 and 1.98x on IC02, and it fell from 37% of the query's time to 13%.

  The plan itself is unchanged, and the receipt proves that rather than asserting it: scans (885 / 1,793) and rows returned (70,927 / 2,702) are IDENTICAL on both pins. Same estimates, same clause order, same strategy choices -- only the cost of arriving at them moved."

 :execute-is-flat-and-that-is-the-point
 "Execute went 1,085 -> 1,215 ms on IC09 (0.89x, slightly worse) and 101 -> 78 ms on IC02 (1.29x, better). Averaging to roughly nothing across two queries is what an unchanged execution path looks like measured twice. `query` did change shape -- it composes a transducer over `query-seq` now instead of filtering a materialised set -- so this is not a pure control, but the two queries disagreeing in direction says whatever it contributes is inside the noise here."

 :method-note
 "Both pins were measured back to back in one window, which is the fix recorded in 2026-08-02-scan-instrumentation.edn after comparing a fresh measurement against a remembered one produced a 7x error.

  It mattered again immediately. The SAME pre-B1 code measured 1,153 ms of IC09 planning in the earlier session and 627 ms here -- the machine was 1.7x busier then. Quoting the earlier number against this one would have claimed 6.5x instead of 3.55x. The PROPORTION held across both sessions (37% of query time either way), which is why proportions and counts are the durable products and milliseconds are not."

 :where-the-time-is-now
 ["IC09: 177 ms planning, 1,215 ms execute. Planning is no longer the thing to look at."
  "9% of execute is inside the store (from the previous receipt); the rest is the join's own bookkeeping -- grouping, hash index construction, unification, set building. That is the remaining target."
  ":query-statistics is still unused. This change made the fallback path cheap; supplying real statistics would skip it entirely. Less urgent now that it is 13% rather than 37%."]

 :caveats
 ["Single run per pin, one start person. Counts are exact; milliseconds are same-window ratios only."
  "The counter around scan* adds per-call overhead identically to both pins (scan counts are equal), so it does not bias this comparison."
  "IC02's execute numbers are small (78-101 ms) and correspondingly noisier than IC09's."]

